content.content:
    "file": "apps/crew/src/lib/crew/imports/xlsx.ts",
    "line": 30,
    "body": "P2: The decompression size cap relies on `file.originalSize` from the ZIP entry header, which is metadata declared by the file producer — it is not guaranteed to match the actual decompressed output. A crafted `.xlsx` could declare small entry sizes in its headers while compressing to much larger content, bypassing the `MAX_ENTRY_BYTES` / `MAX_TOTAL_BYTES` checks in the filter. Consider additionally checking the byte length of each decompressed entry after `unzipSync` returns.",
    "author": "cubic-dev-ai"
  },
  {
    "file": "apps/crew/src/lib/crew/imports/xlsx.ts",
    "line": 417,
    "body": "P2: A malformed numeric XML entity can throw during decode and fail the whole preview path. Guarding code points before `fromCodePoint` keeps parser behavior in the expected invalid-workbook error flow.",
    "author": "cubic-dev-ai"
  },
  {
    "file": "apps/crew/src/lib/crew/imports/xlsx.ts",
    "line": 136,
    "body": "P2: Imports can come back empty when the first workbook sheet is not a worksheet. The resolver currently follows the first `<sheet>` relationship blindly; selecting the first relationship with worksheet type would avoid skipping valid data tabs.",
    "author": "cubic-dev-ai"
  },
  {
    "file": "apps/crew/src/components/crew/volunteer-import-flow.tsx",
    "line": 158,
    "body": "P2: Uploading a malformed Excel file can break preview selection because parse errors are not caught in `handleFileChange`. Wrapping `parseCrewImportFile` in `try/catch` and resetting preview state with a toast keeps the form usable when workbook parsing fails.",
    "author": "cubic-dev-ai"
  },
  {
    "file": "apps/crew/src/routes/events/$eventId/heats.tsx",
    "line": 791,
    "body": "P2: A malformed Excel file can break the upload preview flow instead of showing a file issue because client-side parsing is called without a local try/catch. Wrapping `parseCrewImportFile` here and surfacing a user-facing parse error would keep the dialog recoverable for bad workbook content.",
    "author": "cubic-dev-ai"
  },
  {
    "file": "AGENTS.md",
    "line": 153,
    "body": "P2: The 43-line GitNexus configuration block is duplicated verbatim across `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`. These files serve different AI tool audiences, but the GitNexus content is identical. Consider extracting the shared GitNexus content into a single source and referencing it from each file, or adding a maintenance note.",
    "author": "cubic-dev-ai"
  },
  {
    "file": "apps/crew/src/lib/crew/imports/xlsx.ts",
    "line": 344,
    "body": "P2: Time and dateTime formatting discards the seconds component of serial date/time values, causing data loss for cells with second-level precision, e.g. 14:30:45 becomes \"2:30 PM\". Consider adding seconds to the output, at least for the dateTime format.",
    "author": "cubic-dev-ai"
  },
  {
    "file": "apps/crew/src/lib/crew/imports/preview.test.ts",
    "line": 225,
    "body": "P2: The test uses `numFmtId=\"20\"` but expects 12-hour AM/PM output. Per the OOXML spec, numFmtId 20 is `h:mm` and numFmtId 18 is `h:mm AM/PM`. Use `numFmtId=\"18\"` here so the format ID correctly corresponds to the expected \"9:00 AM\" output.",
    "author": "cubic-dev-ai"
  },
  {
    "file": "apps/crew/src/lib/crew/imports/types.ts",
    "line": 31,
    "body": "P3: The `ImportFileRecord` and `ImportFileParseResult` type aliases are exported but never imported or referenced anywhere in the codebase. If these are meant for future use, consider adding a comment or waiting until they are consumed.",
    "author": "cubic-dev-ai"
  },
  {
    "file": "apps/crew/src/lib/crew/imports/tabular.ts",
    "line": 95,
    "body": "P3: Subject-verb agreement is incorrect when `skippedRowCount` is 1 — the message will read \"1 row were skipped\" instead of \"1 row was skipped\". The verb should be conditional on the count to match the noun.",
    "author": "cubic-dev-ai"
  }
]

